# - CACE-LR in the paper is the CACE short-range model plus latent Ewald summation, i.e. the registry method CACE-LES.
# - The errors of the original MLIPs of Refs. [28] (0.8 meV/atom, 60 meV/A), [42] (N2P2: 14 meV/atom, 740 meV/A) and [51] (1 meV/atom, 350 meV/A) are quoted from those papers and not encoded. The pre-fine-tuning errors of the superionic model on the 2000 K set (4.5 meV/atom, 103 meV/A, 0.136 e) are not encoded because their split is not stated; Born-effective-charge RMSEs (e) have no metric property.
# - Other CACE settings (c = 12 channels, l_max = 3, N_embedding, LES sigma = 1 A, k_c = pi) have no hyperparameter individual; the water models use no message passing. The fine-tuned models' settings are those of their base models and are not repeated.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
